
# Audit Planning Memorandum (APM) - Document Structure Template

## Document Metadata (Header)
- Audit Ref: [Reference Code]
- Audit Name: [Name of Audit]
- Prepared By: [Name, Role]
- Organisation: [Organisation Name]

---

## Table of Contents
| Column: Chapter | Column: Content | Column: Page |

---

## Section I: Objective

### Subsection: Audit Objective
- Audit objective statement (narrative paragraph)
- Audit type (e.g., practice audit)
- Audit object reference code
- Methodology description (narrative)

---

## Section II: Background Information

### Subsection: [Audit Topic Name]
- **Previous Audits Table:**
  | Column: Year of Audit | Column: Audit Title | Column: Summary Opinion |

- Narrative description of relevant Group frameworks/models
- Bullet list of governance objectives/purposes
- Strategy description (narrative)
- **Figure(s):** Embedded diagrams/images (e.g., strategic domain frameworks)
- Key assessment points (bullet list)

### Subsection: [Organisation/Entity Name]
- Board/Management responsibilities description (narrative)
- **Figure(s):** Organisational charts (embedded images)
- Reporting structure description (narrative)
- Framework references (e.g., COBIT 2019)

### Subsection: Relevant UK and Group Policies and Functional Rules
- Bullet list of applicable policies/functional rules (e.g., AFRIT, AFIRM, APITIS)

### Subsection: 2nd Line and Other Assurance Providers
- Narrative description of findings from other assurance providers

---

## Section III: Risk Assessment

### Subsection: Consideration of Fraud Risks
- Narrative on fraud risk considerations

### Subsection: Management's Own Assessment of Risks and Controls
- Risk narrative with risk reference code
- **Controls Table:**
  | Column: Control Name | Column: Description | Column: Owner | Column: Previous DET Result | Column: Previous OET Result | Column: Last Test Date |

### Subsection: Key Risks Identified by IA
- Bullet list of identified key risks (risk names/titles)

### Subsection: Local Risk Assessment (Source, Date)
- Risk categories with ratings:
  - Risk Type (e.g., Operational, Reputational, Strategic)
  - Impact level (e.g., High, Moderate, Low)
  - Frequency level (e.g., High, Moderate, Low)

---

## Section IV: Audit Scope Areas

### Subsection: Scope Areas
- **Main Scope Table:**
  | Column: S/N | Column: Audit Area | Column: DET (P/N/A) | Column: OET (P/N/A) |

  Structure: Numbered main areas with lettered sub-areas, each marked with P (Performed) or N/A (Not Applicable) for DET and OET columns.

- **Additional Audit Topics Checkbox Table:**
  | Data Privacy | Outsourcing | ESG |
  | Automation/AI | Sourcing & Procurement | Identity & Access Management |
  | Archiving | End User Computing | BCM |
  | Compliance | | |
  
  Each topic marked as: Applicable / Not Applicable (checkbox style)

### Subsection: Exclusions
- Bullet list of items explicitly out of scope

### Subsection: Audit Period
- Start date to End date

---

## Section V: Data Analytics
- Narrative statement on whether Data Analytics is involved (Yes/No with description)

---

## Section VI: Timeline and Audit Team

### Subsection: GAUD Milestones
- **Milestones Table:**
  | Column: GAUD Milestone | Column: Date | Column: Notes/KPIs |

  Grouped by phases:
  - **Planning phase:** Announcement Letter, Kick-Off Meeting
  - **Fieldwork phase:** APM Approved, AWP Approved, Start of Fieldwork, Exit Meeting/End of Fieldwork
  - **Reporting phase:** Draft Report, Final Draft Report, Final Report
  - **Close Down phase:** Close of Audit

  KPI indicators noted against relevant milestones (KPI 1 through KPI 6)

### Subsection: Audit Team
- **Audit Team Table:**
  | Column: Role | Column: IA Staff Assigned | Column: Budgeted Days |

  Roles include: HIA, IAM, SIA (can be multiple)
  Final row: Total budgeted days

### Subsection: Conflicts of Interest Declaration
- Narrative confirmation statement

---

## Appendix A – Company Structure

- **Embedded Diagram:** Full company/group structure (organisational chart image)
- **Legal Entities in Scope Table:**
  | Column: Holding Company | Column: Legal Entity | Column: In Scope? (Y/N) |

  Grouped by parent holding company, listing all subsidiaries with Y/N scope indicator.

